{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "008C", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:86dbf9db9b76b96501833617478092b0dd9d935c04e155c313e9b8fdaa1e924e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:792283c3e610503c8a46b8dd55f74574a648aad68f0ba33a5481581900b3df67", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt is sometimes convenient to think about <MATH_0001>-maps\ninstead of maps between sheaves either on <MATH_0002> or on <MATH_0003>.\nWe define composition of <MATH_0004>-maps as follows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:82bf1e7f338fb7bb4d9a800c78864efccfb594893d5b62e507aaf237b85de0d3", "unit_id": "tag:008C:prose-0006"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "008C", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$g : Y \\to Z$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0006": "$Y$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{H}$", "MATH_0008": "$Z$", "MATH_0009": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0010": "$f$", "MATH_0011": "$\\psi : \\mathcal{H} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0012": "$g$", "MATH_0013": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0014": "$\\psi$", "MATH_0015": "$(g \\circ f)$", "MATH_0016": "$\\varphi \\circ \\psi$", "MATH_0017": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{H}(W) \\ar[rr]_{(\\varphi \\circ \\psi)_W}\n\\ar[rd]_{\\psi_W} & &\n\\mathcal{F}(f^{-1}g^{-1}W) \\\\\n&\n\\mathcal{G}(g^{-1}W)\n\\ar[ru]_{\\varphi_{g^{-1}W}}\n}\n$$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-composition-f-maps}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0d872cd4bf4f0b14c562ed9f8732efee73cb40bebadf1e3d6c3efbad25428978", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5bf4e83a986ea238c2ea44654fdcc8ea50f742f334e6369cdbc7dc31d9c48b37", "source_text": "Suppose that <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> are continuous\nmaps of topological spaces. Suppose that <MATH_0003> is\na sheaf on <MATH_0004>, <MATH_0005> is a sheaf on <MATH_0006>, and\n<MATH_0007> is a sheaf on <MATH_0008>.\nLet <MATH_0009> be an <MATH_0010>-map.\nLet <MATH_0011> be an <MATH_0012>-map.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>composition of <MATH_0013> and <MATH_0014><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is the\n<MATH_0015>-map <MATH_0016> defined\nby the commutativity of the diagrams\n<MATH_0017>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:68ae2f0dfa1cfc3154dbac31059a833b1bbe79a6546d5f6d1563adb48ebd953d", "unit_id": "tag:008L:statement"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "008C", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\varphi \\circ \\psi$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\mathcal{H}\n\\xrightarrow{\\psi}\ng_*\\mathcal{G}\n\\xrightarrow{g_*\\varphi}\ng_* f_* \\mathcal{F} = (g \\circ f)_* \\mathcal{F}\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\varphi_x : \\mathcal{G}_{f(x)} \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{F}_x\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0009": "$(V, s)$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{G}_{f(x)}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{F}_x$", "MATH_0012": "$(f^{-1}V,\n\\varphi_V(s))$", "MATH_0013": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{F}(f^{-1}V) \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{F}_x \\\\\n\\mathcal{G}(V) \\ar[r] \\ar[u]^{\\varphi_V} &\n\\mathcal{G}_{f(x)} \\ar[u]^{\\varphi_x}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0014": "$f(x) \\in V \\subset Y$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7beb00d6fb81f04ece06ae826e9318138d99939ecea1ab939ec9bef0d69da886", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ae1183a04804782063dfa8043febcfcf0e18484e2f687eda38b3bbeacbe654a1", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe leave it to the reader to verify that this works.\nAnother way to think about this is to think of\n<MATH_0001> as the composition\n<MATH_0002>\nNow, doesn't it seem that thinking about <MATH_0003>-maps is somehow\neasier?\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nFinally, given a continuous map <MATH_0004>, and an\n<MATH_0005>-map <MATH_0006> there is\na natural map on stalks\n<MATH_0007>\nfor all <MATH_0008>. The image of a representative <MATH_0009>\nof an element in <MATH_0010> is mapped to the\nelement in <MATH_0011> with representative <MATH_0012>. We leave it to the reader to see that this\nis well defined. Another way to state it is that it is the\nunique map such that all diagrams\n<MATH_0013>\n(for <MATH_0014> open) commute.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7ee075dbe76918400addf4120dbaaaf468e653e852c286392ed264fcb1a7bbbc", "unit_id": "tag:008C:prose-0007"}
